1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,140
What if you shrank down and walked inside a computer chip?

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:05,148
First, a city of copper.

3
00:00:05,148 --> 00:00:09,141
Tens of kilometers of wiring, stacked about fifteen levels deep.

4
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:10,994
Then the transistors.

5
00:00:10,994 --> 00:00:13,937
Ninety-two billion of them in one laptop chip.

6
00:00:13,937 --> 00:00:16,497
More than ten for every person on Earth.

7
00:00:16,983 --> 00:00:21,957
It's sold as a three-nanometer chip, but nothing in it is three nanometers wide.

8
00:00:21,957 --> 00:00:25,003
The gates are about forty-eight nanometers apart.

9
00:00:25,517 --> 00:00:29,069
And the insulating walls once got so thin, about five atoms,

10
00:00:29,069 --> 00:00:31,792
that electrons tunneled straight through them.

11
00:00:32,283 --> 00:00:34,388
So what would you actually see down there?

12
00:00:34,388 --> 00:00:35,691
Full story on the channel.
